Don't let rename() replace a file with a directory.
When the target of a rename existed, mingw_rename() fell back to
MoveFileEx() with MOVEFILE_REPLACE_EXISTING, which replaces a file even
when the source is a directory, so "mv dir file" deleted the file.
POSIX requires rename() to fail with ENOTDIR in that case, and mv then
reports it. Check for it before calling MoveFileEx().

---
 win32/mingw.c |    5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

--- a/win32/mingw.c
+++ b/win32/mingw.c
@@ -1277,6 +1277,11 @@
 			return 0;
 		if (errno != EEXIST)
 			return -1;
+		/* MoveFileEx() would replace a file with a directory */
+		if (mingw_is_directory(pold) && !mingw_is_directory(pnew)) {
+			errno = ENOTDIR;
+			return -1;
+		}
 	}
 	if (MoveFileEx(pold, pnew,
 				MOVEFILE_REPLACE_EXISTING | MOVEFILE_COPY_ALLOWED))
